## 2. Definitions

### 2.1. Licensor
"Licensor" means Radomir Kukla with respect to the Original Work and, with respect to a Contribution, the person or legal entity that lawfully submits that Contribution under this License.

### 2.2. You
"You" means the individual or legal entity exercising rights under this License.

### 2.3. Original Work
"Original Work" means the Source Code and related materials first made available by Radomir Kukla under this License.

### 2.4. Source Code
"Source Code" means the preferred form of the Work for making modifications, including, where applicable:

1. program source files;
2. build scripts;
3. project and configuration files;
4. interface definitions;
5. scripts used to control compilation and installation;
6. source assets required to create the Work;
7. documentation included in the repository;
8. dependency manifests and lock files; and
9. other materials reasonably necessary to build, study, test, modify, or distribute the Work.

Source Code does not include third-party materials that are clearly identified as being governed by a separate license.

### 2.5. Object Code
"Object Code" means any non-source form of the Work, including executables, binaries, libraries, installers, packages, archives, bytecode, intermediate code, and compiled assets.

### 2.6. Work
"Work" means the Original Work, any Modified Work, any Contribution, and any covered portion of them.

### 2.7. Modified Work
"Modified Work" means any work based upon, derived from, adapted from, incorporating, linking with, or modifying all or any copyrightable portion of the Work, where permission from a copyright holder would be required under applicable law.

Mere aggregation of independent and separate works on the same storage medium or distribution service does not, by itself, create a Modified Work.

### 2.8. Fork
"Fork" means a publicly or privately maintained copy of the repository that has been separated from, derived from, or developed independently of the Original Repository.

### 2.9. Original Repository
"Original Repository" means the repository designated by the Licensor as the primary official source-code repository for the Original Work.

### 2.10. Contribution
"Contribution" means any intentional submission of source code, documentation, assets, patches, commits, pull requests, or other copyrightable material intended for inclusion in the Work.

### 2.11. Contributor
"Contributor" means a person or legal entity that submits a Contribution included in the Work.

### 2.12. Distribution
"Distribute" or "Distribution" means to provide, publish, transmit, communicate, host, share, sublicense, or otherwise make a copy of the Work available to any third party.

Distribution includes making the Work available through a public repository, private repository accessible by third parties, download service, package registry, application store, network service, or physical medium.

### 2.13. Non-Commercial Purpose
"Non-Commercial Purpose" means a purpose that is exclusively personal, educational, academic, private, hobbyist, archival, preservation-oriented, or otherwise not commercial in nature.

A purpose is not a Non-Commercial Purpose if it is directly or indirectly connected to a commercial activity, commercial benefit, or for-profit business operation.

### 2.14. Commercial Use
"Commercial Use" means any use of the Work that is not exclusively for a Non-Commercial Purpose.

Commercial Use includes, without limitation, any use of the Work:

1. to generate revenue, reduce costs, support sales, improve a business, or obtain commercial advantage;
2. by, for, on behalf of, or in support of a for-profit business;
3. in connection with a product, service, platform, app, game, website, tool, or offering that is sold, licensed, subscribed to, sponsored, monetized, or otherwise made available for commercial benefit;
4. in internal business operations, research, development, testing, quality assurance, deployment, security review, training, support, consulting, integration, maintenance, or demonstration for a business or client;
5. to provide paid services, including hosting, software-as-a-service, managed service, consulting, development, customization, support, integration, or maintenance;
6. to fulfill work performed for compensation, whether for a client, employer, contractor, or other paying party;
7. to market, promote, validate, improve, or operate another commercial product or service;
8. in exchange for payment, fees, subscriptions, advertising, sponsorship, paid memberships, paid access, or commercial data collection; or
9. in any distribution or publication intended to support or promote a commercial activity.

Receiving voluntary donations that are not required in exchange for access to the Work does not, by itself, constitute Commercial Use, provided that the Work is not otherwise used for commercial advantage and no paid feature, access tier, benefit, or service is offered in return.

### 2.15. Corresponding Source
"Corresponding Source" means all Source Code needed to generate, install, execute, understand, test, and modify a distributed version of the Work, including the scripts and configuration files used to control those activities.

Corresponding Source includes, to the extent part of the Work:

1. the complete Source Code of the version being distributed;
2. build scripts and packaging scripts;
3. configuration files;
4. lock files and dependency manifests;
5. source assets and other materials needed to rebuild the distributed version; and
6. documentation reasonably necessary to build, install, and modify the Work.

Corresponding Source does not include general-purpose tools or system components normally available independently of the Work, unless those tools or components are themselves part of the Work.

### 2.16. Complete Contributor Record
"Complete Contributor Record" means a reasonably accurate record identifying all Contributors credited in the Original Repository up to the applicable Synchronization Date.

The record should include, where available in the Original Repository:

- names or established pseudonyms;
- contribution attributions;
- relevant copyright notices;
- authorship information preserved in the repository;
- the date or commit used as the attribution snapshot; and
- a reference to the Original Repository.

No Contributor is required to disclose a legal name, email address, or other personal information that the Contributor did not publicly use for attribution.

### 2.17. Synchronization Date
"Synchronization Date" means:

1. for a Fork that does not later incorporate changes from the Original Repository, the date or commit at which the Fork was created or last synchronized;
2. for a Fork that later merges, rebases, cherry-picks, copies, or otherwise incorporates changes from the Original Repository, the date or commit of the most recent such incorporation; or
3. for another Modified Work, the latest date or commit from the Original Repository whose content is included in that Modified Work.

