## 16. Termination

Your rights under this License terminate automatically if You materially violate its terms.

Where the violation is capable of remedy, Your rights are provisionally reinstated if:

1. You cease the violation;
2. You correct the violation in full;
3. You notify affected recipients where reasonably necessary; and
4. You complete the correction within thirty days after discovering the violation or receiving written notice.

The reinstatement becomes permanent if the relevant Licensor does not notify You of a continuing material violation within sixty days after receiving adequate notice of the correction.

Automatic reinstatement is not available for repeated deliberate Commercial Use, intentional removal of authorship information, knowing copyright infringement, or fraudulent representation of an unofficial build as official, unless the affected rights holder expressly agrees otherwise in writing.

Termination does not affect licenses already validly granted by You to recipients who remain in compliance with this License.

